  "articleBody": "It’s easy to get excited about a single-room renovation and jump right in, but there are some common pitfalls that can really cost you time and money. One of the biggest mistakes we see is renovating a room in isolation without a whole-home vision. You might love your new bathroom, but if it clashes with your next-door bedroom, you could regret it later. Another big one is vague specifications. Don't just say 'new floors'; specify the type, color, and finish! This helps ensure everyone is on the same page and bids are accurate. Reactively tracking procurement, meaning you're only checking on orders once they're overdue, is a recipe for delays. Get ahead of it! Also, trying to make decisions too late in the process or underestimating the complexity or lead times for certain materials can really throw off your schedule and budget. For instance, some custom items can take weeks to arrive. If your project involves things like structural changes, updating electrical, plumbing, or if you're unsure about permits, that's when bringing in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC becomes super valuable. We can help you navigate these complexities and avoid those expensive missteps.",
